-- title:
--   Order of the first-branch residue and the ideal (varpi,x,yⁿ)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a level $N \neq 0$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$, modular polynomial data `data` for $q$ (a monic $\Phi$ of degree $\psi(q)$ annihilating $(j,j_q)$) together with the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \bmod q = (Y^q - X)(Y - X^q)$ in the stated bivariate form, integrality hypotheses $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ for the two degeneracy maps from level $N$ to level $Nq$, a place specialization $P$ and a prolongation tuple $R$ over it. Assume $q \nmid N$, that $R$ satisfies `IsModel` (the two divisor laws and the two cusp laws), the order law `OrderLawFixed` at the affine places fixed by the square of geometric Frobenius, and, for a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$ all of which are supersingular (rational, affine, with $j$-value in the supersingular set), the regularity law and the node value law. Let $K \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ and $w \in W$, and assume every $a \in k$ with $a^{q^2} = a$ lies in the image of the reduction $red$ restricted to $A \cap K$. Let $c = (x,y)$ be node coordinates at $w$ over $K$: elements of the node ring $S = R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\ K\ w$ (those functions at level $Nq$ integral for both prolongations, integral at every place above $w$ under the first reduction, and with Laurent expansion in the subfield generated by $K$-constants and $j$, $j_{Nq}$) with first residue of $x$ zero, second residue of $x$ of order $1$ at the Frobenius translate of $w$, second residue of $y$ zero, and first residue of $y$ of order $1$ at $w$. Let $\varpi \in A \cap K$ be such that an element of $A \cap K$ reduces to $0$ exactly when it is a multiple of $\varpi$ in $A \cap K$. Then for every $g \in S$ and every $n \in \mathbb{N}$: the first-component residue $R.\mathrm{nodeResidue}_1\ w\ g$ vanishes or has order at least $n$ at $w$ if and only if $g$ lies in the ideal of $S$ generated by the constant $\varpi$, by $x$ and by $y^n$.
--
--   This is the local normal-crossing (node) description of the $K$-rational node ring of $X_0(Nq)$ at a supersingular place: the filtration by order of vanishing along the first branch is matched with the ideals $(\varpi, x, y^n)$. It is the quantitative form of the case $n$ arbitrary of the vanishing criterion for the first residue, and it feeds the two results producing inertia-fixed node coordinate presentations.
